-- title:
--   An arithmetic contradiction for large mixed coefficients
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge4$ and let $A,B$ be real numbers with $A,B\ge80\,d(d+1)^2$. Then it is impossible that
--   $$
--   \frac{AB}2\le4d(d+1)\bigl(A+B+10\,d(d+1)^2\bigr).
--   $$
--
--   A product of two large numbers outgrows any bound linear in them.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/CoefficientArithmetic.lean#L10-L36

